fact WorkItem(id: "WI-226", description: some(value: "Operation-call-model: two compile-time caches (structural requires_chain + SLD resolution) and binding-aware projection slot matching. Performance and correctness gaps in the pre-WI-226 codebase: (i) requires_chain(spec_sort) re-walks SortRequiresInfo facts from scratch on every defer/Pin-now call site; (ii) dispatch_spec_op_with_tree re-walks SortProvidesInfo candidates from scratch on every spec-op call site even when the same (spec, bindings) has already resolved earlier in the same body; (iii) Strategy 1 and Strategy 2 in build_dep_projection compare entries by required_sort only, so a caller with Eq[T=X] at slot 0 and a callee needing Eq[T=Y] wrongly emits requirement_at_current(slot=0). Scope: (a) Cache A — requires_chain_cache on KnowledgeBase: RefCell<HashMap<Symbol, Rc<Vec<RequiresEntry>>>> populated lazily by requires_chain. Top-level memoization only (recursive sub-frames bypass the cache because cycle-truncated sub-results can't be canonicalized). Key = Symbol (sort) because the structural chain doesn't depend on bindings — substitution into a caller's per-call subst happens at projection time, not in the cache. (b) Cache B — resolve_cache on KnowledgeBase: RefCell<HashMap<(SortGoal, Vec<RequiresEntry>), (DispatchOutcome, Option<ResolvedTree>)>> populated by a new dispatch_spec_op_cached entry point that wraps the existing dispatch_spec_op_with_tree. Key = (goal, scope) — both must match for a cache hit because FromScope short-circuits change the result. (c) Binding-aware slot matching: replace required_sort-only checks in build_dep_projection's Strategy 1 / Strategy 2 with the entries_cover predicate that compares (required_sort, type-param bindings) via dispatch_values_match. List[X] vs List[Y] now resolve to different slots (or fall through to Strategy 3 if neither covers the dep). Out of scope (split as WI-229 / WI-230): let-binding hoist for repeated projection IR (WI-229); converting requires_chain from flat Vec<RequiresEntry> to tree-structured Vec<RequireNode> (WI-230); factor-out into kb/req_insertion.rs (deferred — more natural after WI-230's tree refactor). Acceptance: cargo-test green; new tests pin (1) requires_chain second call hits cache (HashMap lookup); (2) dispatch_spec_op second call at same (goal, scope) hits cache; (3) caller with Eq[T=X] and dep Eq[T=Y] does NOT match slot 0 (regression for binding-blindness). Reference: docs/design/operation-call-model.md §'Pass structure'."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-222", "WI-227"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-11T22:46:49Z"))
